      "updated": 1793992224431,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why do we need Docker Volumes?",
      "rawText": "Why do we need Docker Volumes?",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why do we need Docker Volumes?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "hasTextLink": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jQPqy9zA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -246.60003662109375,
      "y": -28.600006103515625,
      "width": 1074.5191650390625,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1513373062,
      "version": 60,
      "versionNonce": 627029658,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793992215841,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> Data stored inside a container's writable layer is temporary and can be lost when the container is removed.\n-> We need a mechanism to store container data permanently, even after the container is stopped or deleted.\n-> We also need to transfer or share data between the local machine and Docker containers.\n-> Docker Volumes solve these problems by providing persistent storage outside the container's lifecycle.",
      "rawText": "-> Data stored inside a container's writable layer is temporary and can be lost when the container is removed.\n-> We need a mechanism to store container data permanently, even after the container is stopped or deleted.\n-> We also need to transfer or share data between the local machine and Docker containers.\n-> Docker Volumes solve these problems by providing persistent storage outside the container's lifecycle.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> Data stored inside a container's writable layer is temporary and can be lost when the container is removed.\n-> We need a mechanism to store container data permanently, even after the container is stopped or deleted.\n-> We also need to transfer or share data between the local machine and Docker containers.\n-> Docker Volumes solve these problems by providing persistent storage outside the container's lifecycle.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "hasTextLink": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TGBBX9JO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 124.33807373046875,
      "y": 146.0999755859375,
      "width": 355.515869140625,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1051568326,
